{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.AlgebraicGeometricDilogEquivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.AlgebraicGeometricDilogEquivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.algebraic_geometric_equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.algebraic_geometric_equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L318-L332","doc":"**Stated equivalence (conjecture bundle, both halves).**  §1 is the\nunconditional strengthened pole side (`denomPolyLocal_roots_explicit`,\nneeding only `q ≠ 0`); §2 is derived from the class hypotheses.  The\nonly conjectural inputs are the class fields — the composition\ncontains no `sorry` and assumes nothing provable-outright. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence","label":"conj:algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.asymptotic_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.asymptotic_volume","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L305-L316","doc":"**§2 asymptotic, DERIVED from the class hypotheses.**  Given the\naxiomatised inputs (`shape`, `vc_asymptotic`, `pole_cusp_matched`), the\nrescaled log partial product converges to the Bloch-Wigner volume at the\ninstance's matched shape — the conclusion the previous class revision\ncarried as a field, now a theorem via `asymptotic_volume_of_vc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.asymptotic_volume_of_vc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.asymptotic_volume_of_vc","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L290-L303","doc":"**Conditional (VC + pole-cusp match ⟹ §2 asymptotic).** If the q-Pochhammer\nrescaled log converges to a volume `V` (the volume-conjecture saddle\nasymptotic; a theorem for `4₁`) and `V = D(z)` at the matched shape `z ∈ ℍ`\n(the pole-cusp matched cusp volume), then the §2 Bloch–Wigner asymptotic\nholds. The content is the two hypotheses; the composition is a limit-point\nsubstitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_roots_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_roots_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L246-L265","doc":"**Theorem-backed pole side.** The strengthened §1 statement the class field\nomits: the explicit root function `k ↦ q^{-k}` together with the proof that\neach value is a genuine zero of `(x; q)_n`. Unconditional for `q ≠ 0`.\n\n**Renamed 2026-09-14 from `pole_cusp_bijection_proved`** (bean `qou-mfdq`,\nexecuting the recommendation of\n`docs/audits/2026-09-04-how-the-hyperbolic-volume-could-arise-from-qou.md`\n§\"Two moves\"). The old name asserted three things this statement does not\ncontain: there is **no cusp** in the type, **no bijection** (no `Equiv`, no\ninjectivity, no cardinality), and `_proved` claimed a compound the file's own\nprose calls open. What it proves is that `n` explicit values are roots of a\npolynomial. The old name was the sort of thing a downstream reader greps and\ncites as evidence for the geometric side; the corpus-grep discipline is\nexactly what it would have defeated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_eq_zero_at_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_eq_zero_at_pole","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L230-L244","doc":"**Pole vanishing (theorem).** `(x; q)_n` vanishes at each pole `x = q^{-j}`,\n`j < n` (`q ≠ 0`) — the unconditional algebraic half of\n`conj:algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence §1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal_succ","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L226-L228","doc":"Structural unfold of the `n+1` step (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.pole_cusp_matched","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.pole_cusp_matched","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L212-L212","doc":"Hypothesis (ii): the saddle volume is the Bloch-Wigner volume at\nthe matched shape parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.vc_asymptotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.vc_asymptotic","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L205-L205","doc":"Hypothesis (i): the volume-conjecture saddle asymptotic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.volume","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L202-L202","doc":"The limit of the rescaled log partial product (the saddle\nvolume). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.shape","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L199-L199","doc":"The matched ideal-tetrahedron shape parameter (upper half plane;\na real shape would be a flat tetrahedron — see\n`flat_shape_has_no_volume`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence","kind":"class","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L165-L212","doc":"The algebraic-geometric equivalence, as a §3b-cond\nhypothesis-carrying class over the substrate parameter `q` and the\nstate variable `x` (both real; each instance pins one `(q, x)` pair).  Per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond rule 5, the fields axiomatise the conjecture's\n*inputs* — NOT its conclusion:\n\n* (`shape`) the matched ideal-tetrahedron **shape parameter**, on\n  the open upper half plane.  This is the narrative's `z(x)`, no\n  longer \"composed away\": an instance must exhibit the matching\n  map's value, and cannot exhibit a flat (real) one.\n\n* (`vc_asymptotic`) the volume-conjecture **saddle asymptotic**:\n  the rescaled log partial product converges to some limit\n  `volume` under Faddeev's scaling.  This is the analytic core of\n  Kashaev-Murakami-Murakami; for the figure-eight `4₁` it is the\n  theorem of Ohtsuki (2016) / Andersen-Hansen.\n\n* (`pole_cusp_matched`) the matched-cusp volume identification\n  `volume = D(shape)`, whose geometric content is supplied by\n  `conj:shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy` (the pole side of the\n  matching is the unconditional theorem\n  `denomPolyLocal_roots_explicit` below).\n\nThe §2 Bloch-Wigner asymptotic is then **derived**\n(`AlgebraicGeometricEquivalence.asymptotic_volume`), not assumed.\nA previous revision carried the conclusion itself as a field plus\na vacuous `∃ z, z k = q^{-k}` pole field; both are gone — the\nclass now asserts exactly the open hypotheses and nothing\nprovable-outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.shape_ne_zero_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.shape_ne_zero_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L154-L163","doc":"**`UpperHalfPlane` already carries the sibling's shape nondegeneracy.**\nThe sibling conjecture `conj:shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy` encodes a\ncusp shape as a three-field `GeometricShape z` (`z ≠ 0`, `z ≠ 1`,\n`0 < Im z`).  The last field implies the other two — both `0` and `1` are\nreal — so `ℍ` is exactly that predicate and no bespoke structure is needed\nhere.  (The two nondegeneracy fields in the sibling are therefore\nredundant; recorded, not changed, since that file is a separate conjecture\nblock.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.shape_ne_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.shape_ne_real","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L144-L152","doc":"**The upper half plane excludes flat shapes.**  No point of `ℍ` is\na real number, so the retyped `BlochWignerD` cannot be applied to\na flat shape at all: the degeneracy is now a *type* error rather\nthan a derivable `volume = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.flat_shape_has_no_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.flat_shape_has_no_volume","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L129-L142","doc":"**A real shape carries no volume.**  If the volume `V` is named by\na conjugation-antisymmetric `D` at a *real* argument, then `V = 0`\n— the flat tetrahedron.  This is the defect the old\n`BlochWignerD : ℝ → ℝ` typing produced, recorded as a theorem so\nthat reverting the retyping reinstates a visible contradiction\nrather than a silent one.  The corpus's concrete counterpart is\n`QOU.Knot.FlatTet.BlochWigner_lob_ofReal`, which needs no\nantisymmetry hypothesis because `BlochWigner_lob` is defined\nrather than opaque. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.eq_zero_of_conjAntisymm_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.eq_zero_of_conjAntisymm_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L115-L127","doc":"**A conjugation-antisymmetric real-valued function vanishes on ℝ.**\nBloch-Wigner satisfies `D(z̄) = −D(z)`; hence `D` is identically\nzero on the real axis.  (Stated for a general `D` so the file\nstays self-contained; the same statement is proved for the\ncorpus's Bloch volume leg in\n`QOU.MassTheory.BlochVolumeLegFlatVanishing`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.blochWignerD_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.blochWignerD_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L103-L108","doc":"**The discharge is definitional.**  `BlochWignerD` unfolds to the\ncorpus's concrete Bloch-Wigner on the underlying complex point;\nnothing about the conjecture is hidden behind an `opaque` any\nmore. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.BlochWignerD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.BlochWignerD","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L88-L101","doc":"Bloch-Wigner placeholder.  Like `LiTwo`, this stands in for the\nreal-valued `Real.dilog`-derived Bloch-Wigner function `D(z)`\nuntil Mathlib provides a complete formalisation of the classical\ndilogarithm.\n\n**Domain.** `D` is the volume of the ideal tetrahedron of shape\n`z`, so its argument is a shape parameter on the open upper half\nplane, not a real number.  See the module docstring: on `ℝ` the\nfunction vanishes identically, so typing it `ℝ → ℝ` silently\nforces every volume it names to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.partialProductLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.partialProductLocal","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L83-L86","doc":"Local restatement of the partial product `Φ_n(x; q) = 1 / (x; q)_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.denomPolyLocal","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence.lean#L75-L81","doc":"Local restatement of the q-Pochhammer denominator (mirrors the\nsibling `q-pochhammer-partial-product.lean`; kept self-contained\nso this file does not depend on cross-file elaboration). ","signatureChunk":0}]}